      "text": "On the Reading Order of This Very Document\n\n[A1] This paper is a test fixture. [A2] If you are reading the abstract first and the title before it, your pipeline has handled the spanning header correctly. [A3] Everything below is arranged in two columns, and the correct order is the entire left column, top to bottom, followed by the entire right column.\n\n[S01] This is the first paragraph, and it sits at the top of the left column. [S02] A pipeline that reads horizontally across both columns will splice this sentence together with one from the right-hand side and produce nonsense.\n\nright column, where a correct pipeline must rejoin it with the words that follow.\n\n[S06] Those words are these: you are now in the right column, and S05 should have ended just before this sentence began. [S07] If S06 appears before S05 in your output, you read the right column first.\n\n[S03] This is the second paragraph, still in the left column. [S04] The word \"third\" should never appear before the word \"second\" in your output, and the marker S03 should always precede S04.\n\n[S08] This is the fifth paragraph. [S09] A hyphenated line break, such as \"recon-\n\n[S05] This is the third paragraph, and it ends the left column, so its final sentence deliberately runs past the bottom of the column and continues at the top of the\n\n[S10] This is the final paragraph, and it is the last thing in the document. [S11] If this sentence is the last one in your output, the test passes."
